{
  "name": "loach",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/loach.py): a stone loach, 11 cm -- a small SLIM bottom fish, round in front and flattened toward the tail, a small head with a little UNDERSLUNG mouth ringed by SIX short BARBELS (`horn`s), small eyes set high; a rounded dorsal mid-back over the pelvics, a rounded anal, broad low pectorals it props itself on, a nearly square spotted tail; olive-brown, MOTTLED (the coat pattern `mottle`) and blotched with 8 dark irregular saddles, a pale belly. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A SWIMMER that keeps to the bottom (the fish's plumbing).",
